"""synaScriber for openDesk: meeting notes in an openDesk you already run.

  ./synascriber check         what is in your cluster and what would be installed
  ./synascriber plan          preview of every change
  ./synascriber install       install or update Synaplan and meeting notes
  ./synascriber verify        test every piece end to end
  ./synascriber opendesk-env  write the files that keep it through openDesk updates
  ./synascriber uninstall     remove meeting notes (--all: Synaplan as well)

check, plan, verify and opendesk-env change nothing in the cluster.

Options:
  --env FILE   settings file (default: synascriber.env next to this script)
  --yes        do not ask before restarting Jitsi or removing things

Settings: copy synascriber.env.example to synascriber.env. Tools: kubectl,
Helm 3, helmfile, the helm-diff plugin, git, python3 (what openDesk needs).
